OL,3,GNEWSAFamily's 150 years of farming to
OL,4,Aend as site shuts
OL,5,
OL,6,FA family's 150 years of fruit and
OL,7,Fvegetable farming will end later as
OL,8,Ftheir pick-your-own site shuts to the
OL,9,Fpublic for the final time.
OL,11,FGrays Farm in Wokingham, recognised by
OL,12,Fgenerations for its giant fibreglass
OL,13,Fstrawberry, has been run by the Gray
OL,14,Ffamily since 1969 and open to the
OL,15,Fpublic since 1973.
OL,17,FRun initially by Donald Gray, it has
OL,18,Fbeen looked after by their son Peter,
OL,19,Fhis wife Elizabeth and their son Paul,
OL,20,Fover recent years.
OL,23,APub: 31-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
